# Enable pstore/ramoops so kernel log output survives a crash, panic, or
# watchdog reset -- readable from /sys/fs/pstore/ after the *next* boot,
# independent of whether serial or USB networking was working at the time
# of the failure. The reserved-memory ramoops@44410000 node already exists
# in dts/0001 (matches the vendor's own pstore region for dual-boot safety)
# but CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM was never enabled to actually back it -- see
# blockers.md B-17, 2026-07-08.
CONFIG_PSTORE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_RAM=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_CONSOLE=y
CONFIG_PSTORE_PMSG=y
#
# CONFIG_PSTORE_FTRACE was listed here and never took effect: it depends on
# FUNCTION_TRACER, which is off, so merge_config asked for it and olddefconfig
# quietly dropped it every build since this fragment was written (found
# 2026-08-21 when gemini-kbuild.sh started asserting that fragment symbols
# survive). Enabling FUNCTION_TRACER means mcount instrumentation on every
# kernel function, on a device whose boot timing is load-bearing — the
# watchdog has to probe by ~0.62 s. The persistent kernel log above is what
# this fragment is actually for; a persistent function trace is not worth that
# on this machine. Removed rather than silently unsatisfied.
